# Power moves to the other guide in lambda / (2 (n_even - n_odd)) = 8.36 um, from the supermodes of the transverse grid.
# Reference: full transfer at that length, half at half of it. Monitors use the modes of the separate guides, which overlap slightly at small gaps.
title Directional coupler, two 0.5 um guides 100 nm apart
window width=14 length=18.75
guide straight x=-0.3 width=0.5 from=0 to=18.75
guide straight x=0.3 width=0.5 from=0 to=18.75
launch mode x=-0.3 width=0.5
monitor half_cross z=4.25 x=0.3 width=0.5
monitor cross_full z=8.25 x=0.3 width=0.5
monitor bar_full z=8.25 x=-0.3 width=0.5
monitor bar_end z=18.75 x=-0.3 width=0.5
monitor cross_end z=18.75 x=0.3 width=0.5
expect power half_cross 0.509489396 2e-7
expect power cross_full 0.994402871 2e-7
expect power bar_full 0.011591783 2e-7
expect power bar_end 0.848719694 2e-7
expect power cross_end 0.146094149 2e-7
expect neff 2.675559859 2e-8
expect power_above cross_full 0.99
expect power_below bar_full 0.015
expect power half_cross 0.5 0.02
expect sum bar_end cross_end 1.0 0.01
